elop a pool of qualified candidates.  To apply for a position, click on the position of interest and click “Apply” at the bottom of the screen. Delaware Valley University students can apply for student employment (opens in a new window) here. (opens in a new window) Please note, our application process works best when used with Google Chrome as your browser. Get Started Apply to DelVal Request Information Visit DelVal Delvaware Valley University 700 E. Butler Ave.  •  Doylestown, PA 18901 P+ 1.800.2.DelVal Non-Discrimination Statement: Among the core values of Delaware Valley University is the principle to respect all people. We live this through our commitment to ensure equal opportunity to all. Delaware Valley University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, religion, age, genetic information, protected veteran status, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, or other protected classes under the law, in the administration of any of its educational programs or activities, including but not limited to admissions, financial aid, athletics and employment policies and practices, as required by Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, and other applicable statutes. Information For: Accepted Students Alumni Covid-19 Relief Programs Current Students Safety on Campus Employers and Partners Faculty & Staff Families Guidance and School Counselors Careers at DelVal Library Bookstore (external site, opens in a new window) Academic Calendar Spark Bowl Give To DelVal Campus Status Offices & Departments Student Consumer Information For the Media © 2020 Delaware Valley University. All Rights Reserved. Privacy Policy We use cookies on this site to enhance your user experience. By clicking the accept button, you agree to us doing so. View our privacy policy. Accept No, thanks"
